{"family":"qb-a11-ma-c1","course":"ADV","year":11,"topic":"MA-C1","questions":[{"id":"A11-C1-005","group":"A11-C1-005","dp":"C1.3a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":3,"title":"Product with a root","prompt":"Differentiate $y=x^{3}\\sqrt{2x+1}$, writing your answer as a single fraction in factorised form.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"x^2*(7*x+3)/sqrt(2*x+1)"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Use the product rule with $u = x^3$, $v = \\sqrt{2x+1}$.","$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sqrt{2x+1} = \\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}$.","Put both terms over $\\sqrt{2x+1}$."],"steps":[{"h":"Product rule","d":"$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 3x^{2}\\sqrt{2x+1}+x^{3}\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}$"},{"h":"Common denominator","d":"$= \\dfrac{3x^{2}(2x+1)+x^{3}}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}$"},{"h":"Factorise","d":"$= \\dfrac{x^{2}(7x+3)}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"3*x^2*sqrt(2*x+1)+x^3/(2*sqrt(2*x+1))","why":"Forgot the inner factor 2 in the chain rule for √(2x + 1)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct product rule","line":"3*x^2*sqrt(2*x+1)+x^3/sqrt(2*x+1)"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative of √(2x + 1)","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Single factorised fraction","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-006","group":"A11-C1-006","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient rule","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{x^{2}+1}{x-2}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(x^2-4*x-1)/(x-2)^2"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["$\\left(\\tfrac uv\\right)^\\prime = \\dfrac{vu^\\prime-uv^\\prime}{v^2}$.","$u = x^2+1$, $v = x-2$.","Expand and collect the numerator."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient rule","d":"$\\dfrac{(x-2)(2x)-(x^{2}+1)(1)}{(x-2)^{2}}$"},{"h":"Simplify","d":"$= \\dfrac{x^{2}-4x-1}{(x-2)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"(x^2+4*x+1)/(x-2)^2","why":"Subtracted in the wrong order in the quotient rule."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct quotient rule","line":"((x-2)*2*x-(x^2+1))/(x-2)^2"},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified numerator","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-014","group":"A11-C1-014","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Chain rule with a negative power","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{4-x^{2}}}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"x/(4-x^2)^(3/2)"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Write the root as a power.","Multiply by the inner derivative.","Two negatives make a positive."],"steps":[{"h":"Index form","d":"$y = \\left(4-x^{2}\\right)^{-1/2}$"},{"h":"Chain rule","d":"$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = -\\tfrac12\\left(4-x^{2}\\right)^{-3/2}(-2x) = \\dfrac{x}{\\left(4-x^{2}\\right)^{3/2}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"-x/(4-x^2)^(3/2)","why":"Lost the sign from the inner derivative −2x."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Writes as a power and applies the chain rule","line":"-1/2*(4-x^2)^(-3/2)*(-2*x)"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct simplified answer","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-017","group":"A11-C1-017","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Splitting before differentiating","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{x^{2}-3\\sqrt x+2}{x}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"1+3/2*x^(-3/2)-2/x^2"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Divide each term by x first.","Write roots and fractions as powers.","Differentiate term by term."],"steps":[{"h":"Split","d":"$y = x-3x^{-1/2}+2x^{-1}$"},{"h":"Differentiate","d":"$\\dfrac{dy}{dx} = 1+\\tfrac32x^{-3/2}-2x^{-2}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"1-3/2*x^(-3/2)-2/x^2","why":"Sign slip: the derivative of −3x^{−1/2} is +3/2 x^{−3/2}."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Divides each term by x","line":"x-3*x^(-1/2)+2*x^(-1)"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-020","group":"A11-C1-020","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Tangent to a root curve","prompt":"Find where the tangent to $y=\\sqrt x$ at $x=4$ meets the $x$-axis.","answerType":"point","answer":{"x":-4,"y":0},"hints":["Find the point and gradient at x = 4.","Write the tangent.","Set y = 0."],"steps":[{"h":"Tangent","d":"At $x = 4$: $y = 2$, $y' = \\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt x} = \\tfrac14$, so $y = \\tfrac14x+1$."},{"h":"x-intercept","d":"$0 = \\tfrac14x+1 \\Rightarrow x = -4$"}],"traps":[{"point":[4,0],"why":"Sign slip solving x/4 + 1 = 0."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Tangent y = x/4 + 1","line":"y = x/4+1"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct point","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-022(ii)","group":"A11-C1-022","label":"(ii)","dp":"C1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Growth rate of a town","prompt":"The population of a town, in thousands, $t$ years after 2020 is modelled by $P=500+40t-t^{2}$.\n\nIn which year is the population growing at $10$ thousand per year?","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":2035},"answerPrefix":"year","hints":["Set the derivative equal to 10.","Solve for t.","Convert t to a year."],"steps":[{"h":"Solve","d":"$40-2t = 10 \\Rightarrow t = 15$, the year 2035."}],"traps":[{"value":15,"why":"Gave t, not the year."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct year","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-024","group":"A11-C1-024","dp":"C1.3c","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":3,"title":"Normal parallel to a line","prompt":"Find the point on $y=x^{2}-5x+7$ at which the normal is parallel to the line $x+3y=6$.","answerType":"point","answer":{"x":4,"y":3},"hints":["Find the gradient of x + 3y = 6.","The tangent is perpendicular to the normal.","Set the derivative equal to the tangent gradient."],"steps":[{"h":"Gradients","d":"The normal has gradient $-\\tfrac13$, so the tangent has gradient $3$."},{"h":"Solve","d":"$2x-5 = 3 \\Rightarrow x = 4$, $y = 16-20+7 = 3$"}],"traps":[{"point":[2.33,0.78],"why":"Set the tangent gradient to −1/3 instead of the normal gradient."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Tangent gradient 3","line":"m = 3"},{"marks":1,"point":"x = 4","line":"x = 4"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct point","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-026","group":"A11-C1-026","dp":"C1.3a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":2,"title":"Mixed powers at a point","prompt":"Find $f'(1)$ for $f(x)=3x^{4}-\\dfrac2x+5\\sqrt x$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":16.5},"hints":["Write each term as a power of x.","Multiply by the index and subtract one.","Substitute x = 1."],"steps":[{"h":"Differentiate","d":"$f'(x)=12x^{3}+2x^{-2}+\\tfrac52x^{-1/2}$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$12+2+2.5=16.5$"}],"traps":[{"value":12.5,"why":"The derivative of −2x⁻¹ is +2x⁻²."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","line":"12*x^3+2*x^(-2)+5/2*x^(-1/2)"},{"marks":1,"point":"16.5","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-029","group":"A11-C1-029","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient of quadratics","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{x^{2}+1}{x-1}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(x^2-2*x-1)/(x-1)^2"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["vu′ − uv′ over v².","u = x² + 1 and v = x − 1.","Expand the numerator."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient rule","d":"$\\dfrac{2x(x-1)-(x^{2}+1)}{(x-1)^{2}}$"},{"h":"Simplify","d":"$\\dfrac{x^{2}-2x-1}{(x-1)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"(x^2+2*x+1)/(x-1)^2","why":"Reversed the order in the numerator."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient rule","line":"(2*x*(x-1)-(x^2+1))/(x-1)^2"},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-032","group":"A11-C1-032","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Normal to a root curve","prompt":"Find the equation of the normal to $y=\\sqrt x$ at the point $(4,2)$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"-4*x+18"},"hints":["Differentiate x^{1/2}.","Take the negative reciprocal.","Use the point (4, 2)."],"steps":[{"h":"Tangent gradient","d":"$y'=\\tfrac{1}{2\\sqrt x}=\\tfrac14$"},{"h":"Normal","d":"$y-2=-4(x-4)\\Rightarrow y=-4x+18$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = x/4+1","why":"That is the tangent."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Normal gradient −4","line":"m = -4"},{"marks":1,"point":"y = −4x + 18","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-034","group":"A11-C1-034","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Where the gradient is negative three","prompt":"Find the point on $y=x^{3}-6x^{2}+9x$ where the gradient of the tangent is $-3$.","answerType":"point","answer":{"x":2,"y":2},"hints":["Set y′ = −3.","Rearrange to zero.","Find y."],"steps":[{"h":"Equation","d":"$3x^{2}-12x+9=-3\\Rightarrow(x-2)^{2}=0$"},{"h":"Point","d":"$x=2$, $y=8-24+18=2$"}],"traps":[{"point":[2,-2],"why":"Arithmetic: 8 − 24 + 18 = 2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"(x − 2)² = 0","line":"(x-2)^2 = 0"},{"marks":1,"point":"(2, 2)","answer":true}],"stepcheck":{"kind":"equation","variable":"x","solutions":[2]}},{"id":"A11-C1-040","group":"A11-C1-040","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Reciprocal of a square","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{1}{(2x-1)^{2}}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"-4/(2*x-1)^3"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Write as (2x − 1)⁻².","Chain rule.","Multiply by 2."],"steps":[{"h":"Negative power","d":"$(2x-1)^{-2}$"},{"h":"Chain rule","d":"$-2(2x-1)^{-3}\\cdot2$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"-2/(2*x-1)^3","why":"Forgot the inner derivative 2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Rewrites as a negative power","line":"(2*x-1)^(-2)"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-042","group":"A11-C1-042","dp":"C1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Gradient of a root of a quadratic","prompt":"Find the gradient of $y=\\sqrt{x^{2}+9}$ at $x=4$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.8},"hints":["Write as (x² + 9)^{1/2}.","Chain rule.","√25 = 5."],"steps":[{"h":"Chain rule","d":"$y'=\\dfrac{x}{\\sqrt{x^{2}+9}}$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$\\tfrac45$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.1,"why":"Forgot to multiply by 2x.","expr":"1/10"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","line":"x/sqrt(x^2+9)"},{"marks":1,"point":"4/5","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-044","group":"A11-C1-044","dp":"C1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Cooling water","prompt":"The temperature of water is $T=20+\\dfrac{80}{t+1}$ °C after $t$ minutes. Find the rate of change of temperature at $t=3$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-5},"hints":["Write 80(t + 1)⁻¹.","Differentiate.","Substitute t = 3."],"steps":[{"h":"Differentiate","d":"$T'=-\\dfrac{80}{(t+1)^{2}}$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$-\\tfrac{80}{16}=-5$"}],"traps":[{"value":40,"why":"Gave the temperature, not its rate."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","line":"-80/(t+1)^2"},{"marks":1,"point":"−5 °C/min","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-045","group":"A11-C1-045","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Parallel tangents on two curves","prompt":"For $x>0$, find the value of $x$ at which the tangents to $y=x^{2}$ and $y=x^{3}$ are parallel.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.6666666666666666},"answerPrefix":"x =","hints":["Parallel means equal gradients.","Factorise.","Reject x = 0."],"steps":[{"h":"Equal gradients","d":"$2x=3x^{2}\\Rightarrow x(3x-2)=0$"},{"h":"Positive root","d":"$x=\\tfrac23$"}],"traps":[{"value":0,"why":"x must be positive."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"2x = 3x²","line":"2*x = 3*x^2"},{"marks":1,"point":"x = 2/3","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-046","group":"A11-C1-046","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Tangent parallel to a line","prompt":"Find the point on $y=x^{2}-4x+7$ at which the tangent is parallel to $y=2x+3$.","answerType":"point","answer":{"x":3,"y":4},"hints":["Parallel lines have equal gradients.","Solve y′ = 2.","Use the curve for y."],"steps":[{"h":"Gradient 2","d":"$2x-4=2\\Rightarrow x=3$"},{"h":"Point","d":"$y=9-12+7=4$"}],"traps":[{"point":[3,9],"why":"Substituted into the line, not the curve."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"x = 3","line":"x = 3"},{"marks":1,"point":"(3, 4)","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-051","group":"A11-C1-051","dp":"C1.3a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":2,"title":"Divide before differentiating","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{x^{3}-1}{x}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"2*x+1/x^2"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Divide each term by x.","Write as powers.","Differentiate."],"steps":[{"h":"Split","d":"$x^{2}-x^{-1}$"},{"h":"Differentiate","d":"$2x+x^{-2}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"2*x-1/x^2","why":"The derivative of −x⁻¹ is +x⁻²."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Splits","line":"x^2-x^(-1)"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-052","group":"A11-C1-052","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Tangent to a fourth power","prompt":"Find the equation of the tangent to $y=(x+1)^{4}$ at $x=0$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"4*x+1"},"hints":["Chain rule.","Point at x = 0.","y = mx + c."],"steps":[{"h":"Gradient","d":"$y'=4(x+1)^{3}=4$ at $(0,1)$"},{"h":"Tangent","d":"$y=4x+1$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = 4*x","why":"The point is (0, 1)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Gradient 4","line":"m = 4"},{"marks":1,"point":"y = 4x + 1","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-053","group":"A11-C1-053","dp":"C1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Gradient on a quarter circle","prompt":"Find the gradient of $y=\\sqrt{1-x^{2}}$ at $x=0.6$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-0.75},"hints":["Write as (1 − x²)^{1/2}.","Chain rule.","√(1 − 0.36) = 0.8."],"steps":[{"h":"Chain rule","d":"$y'=\\dfrac{-x}{\\sqrt{1-x^{2}}}$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$\\dfrac{-0.6}{0.8}$"}],"traps":[{"value":-0.6,"why":"Forgot to divide by the root."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","line":"-x/sqrt(1-x^2)"},{"marks":1,"point":"−3/4","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-055","group":"A11-C1-055","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Normal to a parabola","prompt":"Find the equation of the normal to $y=x^{2}-3x$ at $x=1$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"x-3"},"hints":["Find y′ at x = 1.","Negative reciprocal.","Point (1, −2)."],"steps":[{"h":"Tangent gradient","d":"$y'=2x-3=-1$ at $(1,-2)$"},{"h":"Normal","d":"Gradient $1$: $y+2=x-1$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = -x-1","why":"That is the tangent."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Normal gradient 1","line":"m = 1"},{"marks":1,"point":"y = x − 3","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-058","group":"A11-C1-058","dp":"C1.3d","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":3,"title":"Distance in the first four seconds","prompt":"A particle has displacement $x=5t-t^{2}$ metres. Find the total distance travelled in the first $4$ seconds.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":8.5},"hints":["Find when v = 0.","Find positions at the turn and at t = 4.","Add both legs."],"steps":[{"h":"Turn","d":"$v=5-2t=0$ at $t=2.5$"},{"h":"Positions","d":"$x(2.5)=6.25$, $x(4)=4$"},{"h":"Distance","d":"$6.25+2.25=8.5$"}],"traps":[{"value":4,"why":"That is the displacement."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"t = 2.5","line":"t = 2.5"},{"marks":1,"point":"x(2.5) and x(4)","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"8.5 m","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-061","group":"A11-C1-061","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Tangent to a root curve","prompt":"Find the equation of the tangent to $y=\\sqrt{2x+1}$ at $x=4$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"x/3+5/3"},"hints":["Chain rule.","Point (4, 3).","Point-gradient form."],"steps":[{"h":"Gradient","d":"$y'=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2x+1}}=\\tfrac13$ at $(4,3)$"},{"h":"Tangent","d":"$y-3=\\tfrac13(x-4)$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = x/6+7/3","why":"Missed the inner derivative 2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Gradient 1/3","line":"m = 1/3"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct tangent","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-063","group":"A11-C1-063","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Tangent parallel to a given line","prompt":"Find $a$ so that the tangent to $y=x^{2}+ax$ at $x=1$ is parallel to $y=5x$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":3},"answerPrefix":"a =","hints":["y′ = 2x + a.","Parallel means gradient 5.","Solve."],"steps":[{"h":"Gradient","d":"$2+a=5$"}],"traps":[{"value":4,"why":"Used y(1) = 5."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"a = 3","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-065","group":"A11-C1-065","dp":"C1.3b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"A turning point found by the quotient rule","prompt":"Find the gradient of $y=\\dfrac{x}{x^{2}+1}$ at $x=1$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0},"hints":["Quotient rule.","Simplify the numerator.","Substitute x = 1."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient rule","d":"$y'=\\dfrac{1-x^{2}}{(x^{2}+1)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5,"why":"That is y(1)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","line":"(1-x^2)/(x^2+1)^2"},{"marks":1,"point":"0","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-066","group":"A11-C1-066","dp":"C1.3c","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Tangent to a cubic from an outside point","prompt":"Find the equation of the tangent to $y=x^{3}$ that passes through $(0,2)$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"3*x+2"},"hints":["Tangent at a general point a.","Substitute (0, 2).","Solve for a."],"steps":[{"h":"General tangent","d":"At $x=a$: $y=3a^{2}x-2a^{3}$"},{"h":"Through (0, 2)","d":"$-2a^{3}=2\\Rightarrow a=-1$"},{"h":"Tangent","d":"$y=3x+2$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = 2","why":"The tangent at 0 does not pass through (0, 2)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"General tangent","line":"y = 3*a^2*x-2*a^3"},{"marks":1,"point":"a = −1","line":"a = -1"},{"marks":1,"point":"y = 3x + 2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-067","group":"A11-C1-067","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Power of a quadratic","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\left(x^{2}+1\\right)^{3/2}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"3*x*(x^2+1)^(1/2)"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Power rule first.","Inner derivative 2x.","Simplify."],"steps":[{"h":"Chain rule","d":"$\\tfrac32(x^{2}+1)^{1/2}\\cdot2x$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"3/2*(x^2+1)^(1/2)","why":"Forgot the inner 2x."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-068","group":"A11-C1-068","dp":"C1.3a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Reciprocal root","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt x}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"-x^(-3/2)/2"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Write x^{−1/2}.","Multiply by the index.","Subtract 1."],"steps":[{"h":"Power","d":"$x^{-1/2}\\to-\\tfrac12x^{-3/2}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"x^(-1/2)/2","why":"Subtract 1 from −½."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-069","group":"A11-C1-069","dp":"C1.3b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Gradient of a quotient at a point","prompt":"Find the gradient of $y=\\dfrac{x-1}{x+1}$ at $x=1$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.5},"hints":["Quotient rule.","Simplify the numerator.","Substitute x = 1."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient rule","d":"$y'=\\dfrac{2}{(x+1)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0,"why":"That is y(1)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","line":"2/(x+1)^2"},{"marks":1,"point":"½","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-070","group":"A11-C1-070","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Tangent at a root","prompt":"Find the equation of the tangent to $y=x^{2}-x$ where it crosses the positive $x$-axis.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"x-1"},"hints":["Solve x² − x = 0.","Choose the positive root.","Point-gradient form."],"steps":[{"h":"Root","d":"$x=1$"},{"h":"Gradient","d":"$y'=2x-1=1$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = -x","why":"That is at the root x = 0."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Point (1, 0) and gradient 1","line":"m = 1"},{"marks":1,"point":"y = x − 1","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-071","group":"A11-C1-071","dp":"C1.3d","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Velocity from a cubic displacement","prompt":"A particle has displacement $s=4t^{2}-t^{3}$. Find its velocity at $t=2$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":4},"hints":["v = ds/dt.","Differentiate.","Substitute t = 2."],"steps":[{"h":"Differentiate","d":"$v=8t-3t^{2}$"}],"traps":[{"value":8,"why":"That is s(2)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"4","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-072","group":"A11-C1-072","dp":"C1.3e","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Where a cubic decreases","prompt":"For which values of $x$ is $y=x^{3}-12x$ decreasing?","answerType":"interval","answer":{"region":"-2 < x < 2","variable":"x"},"hints":["Decreasing means y′ < 0.","Solve the inequality.","Between the roots."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$y'=3x^{2}-12<0$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$x^{2}<4$"}],"traps":[{"region":"x < -2 or x > 2","why":"That is where it increases."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"3x² − 12 < 0","line":"3*x^2-12 < 0"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct interval","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-075","group":"A11-C1-075","dp":"C1.3a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Second derivative of a power","prompt":"Find $\\dfrac{d^{2}y}{dx^{2}}$ for $y=x^{4}-3x^{2}+2$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"12*x^2-6"},"answerPrefix":"y'' =","hints":["Differentiate once.","Then again.","Constants vanish."],"steps":[{"h":"Twice","d":"$y'=4x^{3}-6x$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"4*x^3-6*x","why":"That is the first derivative."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct second derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-076","group":"A11-C1-076","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Chain rule on a root","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\sqrt{3x^{2}+1}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"3*x/sqrt(3*x^2+1)"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Power ½.","Bring down, reduce power.","Multiply by 6x."],"steps":[{"h":"Chain rule","d":"$\\tfrac12(3x^{2}+1)^{-1/2}\\cdot6x$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"1/(2*sqrt(3*x^2+1))","why":"Multiply by the inner derivative."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-077","group":"A11-C1-077","dp":"C1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Rate of change of volume","prompt":"The volume of a cube of side $x$ cm is $V=x^{3}$. Find the rate of change of $V$ with respect to $x$ when $x=4$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":48},"hints":["Differentiate V.","Substitute x = 4.","3 × 16."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$3x^{2}$ at $4$"}],"traps":[{"value":64,"why":"That is the volume."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"48","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-080","group":"A11-C1-080","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Tangent to a cubic at its intercept","prompt":"Find the equation of the tangent to $y=x^{3}-2x+1$ at its $y$-intercept.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"-2*x+1"},"hints":["x = 0 gives the point.","Differentiate.","Substitute 0."],"steps":[{"h":"Point","d":"$(0,1)$"},{"h":"Gradient","d":"$y'(0)=-2$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = -2*x","why":"Passes through (0, 1)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Gradient −2","line":"m = -2"},{"marks":1,"point":"Tangent","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-082","group":"A11-C1-082","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient rule with a quadratic denominator","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{x}{x^{2}+1}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(1-x^2)/(x^2+1)^2"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["u = x, v = x² + 1.","vu′ − uv′.","Simplify."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient rule","d":"$\\dfrac{(x^{2}+1)-2x^{2}}{(x^{2}+1)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"(x^2-1)/(x^2+1)^2","why":"Numerator order reversed."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient rule","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-084","group":"A11-C1-084","dp":"C1.3d","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Acceleration of a particle","prompt":"A particle has displacement $x=2t^{3}-9t^{2}+12t$. Find its acceleration at $t=2$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":6},"hints":["v = 6t² − 18t + 12.","a = 12t − 18.","t = 2."],"steps":[{"h":"Differentiate twice","d":"$12t-18$"}],"traps":[{"value":0,"why":"That is the velocity at t = 2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"6","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-085","group":"A11-C1-085","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Normal to a cubic at a point","prompt":"Find the equation of the normal to $y=x^{3}-x$ at $x=1$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"-x/2+1/2"},"hints":["Find y′(1).","Negative reciprocal.","Point (1, 0)."],"steps":[{"h":"Tangent gradient","d":"$3-1=2$ at $(1,0)$"},{"h":"Normal","d":"Gradient $-\\tfrac12$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = 2*x-2","why":"That is the tangent."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Normal gradient −½","line":"m = -1/2"},{"marks":1,"point":"Equation","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-089","group":"A11-C1-089","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Product rule with a root","prompt":"Differentiate $y=x\\sqrt{x+1}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(3*x+2)/(2*sqrt(x+1))"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["u = x, v = √(x + 1).","Product rule.","Common denominator."],"steps":[{"h":"Product","d":"$\\sqrt{x+1}+\\dfrac{x}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}$"},{"h":"Combine","d":"$\\dfrac{2(x+1)+x}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"1/(2*sqrt(x+1))","why":"Use the product rule."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Product rule","line":"sqrt(x+1)+x/(2*sqrt(x+1))"},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-090","group":"A11-C1-090","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Tangent with a given gradient on a parabola","prompt":"Find the point on $y=x^{2}-5x+2$ where the tangent is parallel to $y=x+3$.","answerType":"point","answer":{"x":3,"y":-4},"hints":["Parallel means gradient 1.","Solve 2x − 5 = 1.","Find y."],"steps":[{"h":"Gradient","d":"$2x-5=1$"},{"h":"Point","d":"$9-15+2$"}],"traps":[{"point":[3,-2],"why":"Recompute y at x = 3."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"x = 3","line":"x = 3"},{"marks":1,"point":"(3, −4)","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-091","group":"A11-C1-091","dp":"C1.3d","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Velocity from displacement with a root","prompt":"A particle has $x=\\sqrt{t+4}$ for $t\\ge0$. Find its velocity at $t=5$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.16666666666666666},"hints":["Differentiate.","√9 = 3.","½ × ⅓."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t+4}}$ at $t=5$"}],"traps":[{"value":3,"why":"That is the position."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"1/6","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-092","group":"A11-C1-092","dp":"C1.3b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Gradient at a cusp-free point of a quotient","prompt":"Find the gradient of $y=\\dfrac{2x+1}{x-1}$ at $x=2$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-3},"hints":["Quotient rule.","Simplify the numerator.","Substitute x = 2."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient","d":"$\\dfrac{2(x-1)-(2x+1)}{(x-1)^{2}}=\\dfrac{-3}{(x-1)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"value":3,"why":"Numerator is −3."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"−3","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-094","group":"A11-C1-094","dp":"C1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Average rate of change","prompt":"Find the average rate of change of $f(x)=x^{2}+x$ from $x=1$ to $x=4$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":6},"hints":["f(4) = 20.","f(1) = 2.","Divide by 3."],"steps":[{"h":"Chord","d":"$\\dfrac{20-2}{3}$"}],"traps":[{"value":9,"why":"That is f′(4)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"6","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-095","group":"A11-C1-095","dp":"C1.3c","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Equation of a tangent with a negative power","prompt":"Find the equation of the tangent to $y=\\dfrac{4}{x^{2}}$ at $x=2$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"-x+3"},"hints":["Write as 4x⁻².","Differentiate.","Point-gradient."],"steps":[{"h":"Point","d":"$(2,1)$"},{"h":"Gradient","d":"$-8x^{-3}=-1$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = -x+1","why":"Passes through (2, 1)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Gradient −1","line":"m = -1"},{"marks":1,"point":"Tangent","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-097","group":"A11-C1-097","dp":"C1.3d","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Particle changing direction","prompt":"A particle has velocity $v=t^{2}-5t+4$. Find when it changes direction.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[1,4]},"answerPrefix":"t =","hints":["Set v = 0.","Factorise.","v changes sign at single roots."],"steps":[{"h":"Zero","d":"$(t-1)(t-4)=0$"},{"h":"Sign change","d":"Both are single roots"}],"traps":[{"values":[4],"why":"It also turns at t = 1."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Factorises","line":"(t-1)*(t-4) = 0"},{"marks":1,"point":"Both times","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-103","group":"A11-C1-103","dp":"C1.3e","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Gradient function of a sum of powers","prompt":"Find $f'(x)$ for $f(x)=5x^{4}-\\dfrac{3}{x}+7$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"20*x^3+3/x^2"},"answerPrefix":"f'(x) =","hints":["Index form.","Power rule.","Constant vanishes."],"steps":[{"h":"Power rule","d":"$-3x^{-1}\\to3x^{-2}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"20*x^3-3/x^2","why":"Derivative of −3/x is +3/x²."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-104","group":"A11-C1-104","dp":"C1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Rate of change of area of a square","prompt":"Find the rate of change of the area of a square with respect to its side length when the side is $7$ cm.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":14},"hints":["A = s².","dA/ds = 2s.","Substitute."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$2s$"}],"traps":[{"value":49,"why":"That is the area."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"14","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-105","group":"A11-C1-105","dp":"C1.3c","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Tangent and normal through a point","prompt":"Find the point on $y=\\sqrt x$ where the normal has gradient $-4$.","answerType":"point","answer":{"x":4,"y":2},"hints":["Normal −4 means tangent ¼.","Solve 1/(2√x) = ¼.","Find y."],"steps":[{"h":"Tangent gradient","d":"Negative reciprocal of $-4$ is $\\tfrac14$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt x}=\\tfrac14$ gives $x=4$"}],"traps":[{"point":["1/64","1/8"],"why":"That uses 4 as the tangent gradient."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Tangent gradient ¼","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Point","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-106","group":"A11-C1-106","dp":"C1.3e","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Stationary points of a quartic","prompt":"Find the $x$-coordinates of the stationary points of $y=x^{4}-4x^{3}$.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[0,3]},"answerPrefix":"x =","hints":["Differentiate.","Factor 4x².","Solve."],"steps":[{"h":"Factor","d":"$4x^{2}(x-3)=0$"}],"traps":[{"values":[3],"why":"x = 0 is also stationary."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Both","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-111","group":"A11-C1-111","dp":"C1.3a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Differentiate a quotient of linear terms","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{3x-1}{x+2}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"7/(x+2)^2"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Quotient rule.","Expand the numerator.","Simplify."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient rule","d":"$\\dfrac{3(x+2)-(3x-1)}{(x+2)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"5/(x+2)^2","why":"6 + 1 = 7."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-120","group":"A11-C1-120","dp":"C1.3b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient rule with a square on the bottom","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{x^{2}}{x+1}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(x^2+2*x)/(x+1)^2"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["u = x², v = x + 1.","vu′ − uv′.","Over v²."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient rule","d":"$\\dfrac{2x(x+1)-x^{2}}{(x+1)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"(x^2+2*x)/(x+1)","why":"Denominator is squared."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient rule","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-121","group":"A11-C1-121","dp":"C1.3b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Product with a root factor","prompt":"Differentiate $y=(x+2)\\sqrt{x}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(3*x+2)/(2*sqrt(x))"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["u = x + 2, v = √x.","Product rule.","Common denominator."],"steps":[{"h":"Product","d":"$\\sqrt x+\\dfrac{x+2}{2\\sqrt x}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"1/(2*sqrt(x))","why":"Use the product rule."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Product rule","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-122","group":"A11-C1-122","dp":"C1.3b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":1,"title":"Chain rule with a reciprocal root","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x^{2}+1}}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"-x/(x^2+1)^(3/2)"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["Power −½.","Bring down and reduce.","Times 2x."],"steps":[{"h":"Chain","d":"$-\\tfrac12(x^{2}+1)^{-3/2}\\cdot2x$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"-1/(2*(x^2+1)^(3/2))","why":"Multiply by 2x."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-127","group":"A11-C1-127","dp":"C1.3b","authored":5,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient rule giving a horizontal tangent condition","prompt":"For $y=\\dfrac{x+k}{x^{2}+1}$, find $k$ so that the curve has a stationary point at $x=1$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["Quotient rule numerator.","Set zero at x = 1.","Solve."],"steps":[{"h":"Numerator","d":"$(x^{2}+1)-2x(x+k)=1-x^{2}-2kx$"},{"h":"At 1","d":"$-2k=0$"}],"traps":[{"value":1,"why":"Substitute x = 1 into 1 − x² − 2kx."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Numerator of derivative","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"k = 0","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-135","group":"A11-C1-135","dp":"C1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"First principles at a specific point","prompt":"Use first principles to find $f'(2)$ for $f(x)=x^{2}+x$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":5},"hints":["f(2) = 6.","Expand f(2 + h).","Let h → 0."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient","d":"$\\dfrac{(2+h)^{2}+(2+h)-6}{h}=5+h$"}],"traps":[{"value":6,"why":"That is f(2)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Simplifies","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"5","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-141","group":"A11-C1-141","dp":"C1.3d","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Maximum height of a thrown ball","prompt":"A ball has height $h=1.5+14t-4.9t^{2}$ m. Find its maximum height, to one decimal place.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":11.5,"tol":0.05},"hints":["Velocity zero at the top.","Solve for t.","Substitute."],"steps":[{"h":"Stationary","d":"$14-9.8t=0\\Rightarrow t=\\tfrac{10}{7}$"},{"h":"Height","d":"$1.5+20-10$"}],"traps":[{"value":21.5,"why":"Subtract 4.9t²."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"t = 10/7","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"11.5 m","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-143","group":"A11-C1-143","dp":"C1.3d","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Total distance with a turnaround","prompt":"A particle has $x=t^{2}-4t$ for $0\\le t\\le5$. Find the total distance travelled.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":13},"hints":["Find when v = 0.","Positions at 0, 2, 5.","Add distances."],"steps":[{"h":"Turn","d":"$v=0$ at $t=2$, $x=-4$"},{"h":"Distance","d":"$4+9$"}],"traps":[{"value":5,"why":"That is the displacement."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Turns at t = 2","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"13","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-144","group":"A11-C1-144","dp":"C1.3d","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Rate of change of volume in a tank","prompt":"The volume of water in a tank is $V=1000-20t+0.1t^{2}$ L for $0\\le t\\le100$. Find the rate of change at $t=30$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-14},"hints":["Differentiate.","Substitute 30.","Sign."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$-20+0.2t$"}],"traps":[{"value":14,"why":"Volume is decreasing."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"−14","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-155","group":"A11-C1-155","dp":"C1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":1,"title":"Limit evaluated by factorising","prompt":"Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\lim_{x\\to2}\\frac{x^{2}-4}{x-2}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":4},"hints":["Factor the numerator.","Cancel.","Substitute 2."],"steps":[{"h":"Factor","d":"$x+2$"}],"traps":[{"value":0,"why":"Factor before substituting."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"4","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-156","group":"A11-C1-156","dp":"C1.3a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Derivative with fractional powers","prompt":"Find the gradient of $y=\\dfrac{x^{2}+4}{\\sqrt x}$ at $x=4$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":2.75},"hints":["Divide each term by √x.","Power rule.","Substitute 4."],"steps":[{"h":"Split","d":"$x^{3/2}+4x^{-1/2}$"},{"h":"Differentiate","d":"$\\tfrac32x^{1/2}-2x^{-3/2}$ at $4$: $3-\\tfrac14$"}],"traps":[{"value":3,"why":"Include the second term."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Index form","line":"x^(3/2)+4*x^(-1/2)"},{"marks":1,"point":"11/4","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-157","group":"A11-C1-157","dp":"C1.3a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Where two power curves have equal gradient","prompt":"Find the $x$-values where $y=x^{3}$ and $y=6x^{2}-9x$ have equal gradients.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[1,3]},"answerPrefix":"x =","hints":["Differentiate both.","Set equal.","Factor."],"steps":[{"h":"Equate","d":"$3x^{2}=12x-9$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$x^{2}-4x+3=0$"}],"traps":[{"values":[3],"why":"x = 1 also."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Equation","line":"x^2-4*x+3 = 0"},{"marks":1,"point":"Both","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-159","group":"A11-C1-159","dp":"C1.3b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient rule on a linear over a quadratic","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{2x-1}{x^{2}+3}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(-2*x^2+2*x+6)/(x^2+3)^2"},"answerPrefix":"dy/dx =","hints":["u = 2x − 1, v = x² + 3.","vu′ − uv′.","Expand."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient","d":"$\\dfrac{2(x^{2}+3)-2x(2x-1)}{(x^{2}+3)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"(6*x^2-2*x+6)/(x^2+3)^2","why":"Subtract uv′."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient rule","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-160","group":"A11-C1-160","dp":"C1.3b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Chain rule tangent","prompt":"Find the equation of the tangent to $y=(x^{2}-3)^{3}$ at $x=2$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"y","rhs":"12*x-23"},"hints":["Chain rule.","Substitute 2.","Point-gradient."],"steps":[{"h":"Gradient","d":"$3(1)^{2}(4)=12$"},{"h":"Point","d":"$(2,1)$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"y = 3*x-5","why":"Multiply by 2x = 4."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Gradient 12","line":"m = 12"},{"marks":1,"point":"Tangent","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-164","group":"A11-C1-164","dp":"C1.3b","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Chain rule for a rate","prompt":"The radius of a circle is $r=\\sqrt{2t+1}$ cm. Find $\\dfrac{dr}{dt}$ at $t=4$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3333333333333333},"hints":["Power ½.","Times 2.","√9 = 3."],"steps":[{"h":"Chain","d":"$\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{2t+1}}$ at $4$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.16666666666666666,"why":"The 2 cancels the ½.","expr":"1/6"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"⅓","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-166","group":"A11-C1-166","dp":"C1.3d","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":1,"title":"Ball thrown down a well","prompt":"A stone's depth below the top of a well is $d=2t+4.9t^{2}$ m. Find its speed at $t=2$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":21.6},"hints":["Differentiate.","Substitute 2.","Units."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$2+9.8t$"}],"traps":[{"value":23.6,"why":"That is the depth."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"21.6","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-168","group":"A11-C1-168","dp":"C1.3e","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":1,"title":"Function increasing on an interval","prompt":"Find where $y=\\dfrac13x^{3}-x^{2}-8x$ is decreasing.","answerType":"interval","answer":{"region":"-2 < x < 4","variable":"x"},"hints":["y′ = x² − 2x − 8.","Factor.","Negative between."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$(x-4)(x+2)<0$"}],"traps":[{"region":"x > 4","why":"That is increasing."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"−2 < x < 4","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-171","group":"A11-C1-171","dp":"C1.3a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Differentiating a polynomial","prompt":"Differentiate $4x^{3}-2x+7$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"12*x^2-2"},"answerPrefix":"y' =","hints":["Bring the power down.","Reduce the power by 1.","Constants vanish."],"steps":[{"h":"Power rule","d":"Term by term"}],"traps":[{"expr":"12*x^2-2+7","why":"The constant differentiates to 0."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"12x² − 2","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-173","group":"A11-C1-173","dp":"C1.3b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient rule","prompt":"Differentiate $\\dfrac{x}{x+1}$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"1/(x+1)^2"},"answerPrefix":"y' =","hints":["u = x, v = x + 1.","vu′ − uv′ over v².","Simplify."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient rule","d":"$\\dfrac{(x+1)(1)-x(1)}{(x+1)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"-1/(x+1)^2","why":"The order is v u' − u v'."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient rule set up","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-175","group":"A11-C1-175","dp":"C1.3c","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Normal to a root curve","prompt":"Find the equation of the normal to $y=\\sqrt x$ at $x=4$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"-4*x+18"},"answerPrefix":"y =","hints":["Differentiate x^½.","Negative reciprocal.","Use (4, 2)."],"steps":[{"h":"Tangent gradient","d":"$\\tfrac{1}{2\\sqrt4}=\\tfrac14$"},{"h":"Normal gradient","d":"$-4$"},{"h":"Equation","d":"$y-2=-4(x-4)$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"x/4+1","why":"That is the tangent, not the normal."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Tangent gradient","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Normal gradient","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Equation","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-193","group":"A11-C1-193","dp":"C1.3d","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Marginal cost","prompt":"The cost of producing $x$ items is $C=0.01x^{3}-0.6x^{2}+15x$ dollars. Find the marginal cost $\\tfrac{dC}{dx}$ when $x=20$ and interpret it.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":3},"hints":["Differentiate.","Substitute 20.","Cost of one more item."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$0.03x^{2}-1.2x+15$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$12-24+15$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Derivative","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"3","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-195","group":"A11-C1-195","dp":"C1.3b","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient rule with a quadratic numerator","prompt":"Differentiate $\\dfrac{x^{2}+1}{2x-1}$ and simplify.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(2*x^2-2*x-2)/(2*x-1)^2"},"answerPrefix":"y' =","hints":["u = x² + 1, v = 2x − 1.","vu′ − uv′.","Expand."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient rule","d":"$\\dfrac{2x(2x-1)-2(x^{2}+1)}{(2x-1)^{2}}$"},{"h":"Simplify","d":"Expand the numerator"}],"traps":[{"expr":"(2*x^2-2*x+2)/(2*x-1)^2","why":"−2(x² + 1) = −2x² − 2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient rule","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-211","group":"A11-C1-211","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Derivative with expanded brackets","prompt":"Differentiate $y=(2x-1)(x+3)$ by first expanding.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"4*x+5"},"answerPrefix":"y' =","hints":["Expand.","Power rule.","Simplify."],"steps":[{"h":"Expand","d":"$2x^{2}+5x-3$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"4*x+6","why":"The middle term is 5x."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"4x + 5","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-217","group":"A11-C1-217","dp":"C1.3a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Gradient function of a polynomial with negative powers","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{x^{3}-2x+4}{x}$ by first dividing.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"2*x-4/x^2"},"answerPrefix":"y' =","hints":["Divide each term by x.","Power rule.","Sign."],"steps":[{"h":"Divide","d":"$x^{2}-2+4x^{-1}$"},{"h":"Differentiate","d":"$2x-4x^{-2}$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"2*x+4/x^2","why":"d/dx 4x⁻¹ = −4x⁻²."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Divide","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Derivative","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-228","group":"A11-C1-228","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Gradient at a point from a root function","prompt":"Find the gradient of $y=4\\sqrt x$ at $x=9$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.6666666666666666},"hints":["4x^{1/2}.","Power rule.","Substitute 9."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$2x^{-1/2}$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"2/3","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-233","group":"A11-C1-233","dp":"C1.3a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Derivative evaluated at a point","prompt":"If $f(x)=2x^{4}-3x^{2}+x$, find $f'(-1)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-1},"hints":["Power rule.","Substitute −1.","−8 + 6 + 1."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$8x^{3}-6x+1$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"−1","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-235","group":"A11-C1-235","dp":"C1.3c","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Normal to a cubic","prompt":"Find the equation of the normal to $y=x^{3}-4x$ at $x=1$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"x-4"},"answerPrefix":"y =","hints":["y′ = 3x² − 4.","Negative reciprocal.","Point (1, −3)."],"steps":[{"h":"Tangent gradient","d":"$3-4=-1$"},{"h":"Normal","d":"Gradient $1$ through $(1,-3)$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Gradients","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Normal","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-242","group":"A11-C1-242","dp":"C1.3b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient with x squared over x plus one","prompt":"Differentiate $\\dfrac{x^{2}}{x+1}$, simplifying fully.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"x*(x+2)/(x+1)^2"},"hints":["u = x² and v = x + 1.","(vu′ − uv′)/v².","Expand the top."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient","d":"$\\dfrac{2x(x+1)-x^{2}}{(x+1)^{2}}$"},{"h":"Simplify","d":"$\\dfrac{x^{2}+2x}{(x+1)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient rule","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-243","group":"A11-C1-243","dp":"C1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Average rate of change between one and four","prompt":"Find the average rate of change of $f(x)=x^{2}+3x$ between $x=1$ and $x=4$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":8},"hints":["f(4) = 28.","f(1) = 4.","Divide by 3."],"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$\\dfrac{28-4}{3}$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"8","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-253","group":"A11-C1-253","dp":"C1.3b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient with a quadratic denominator plus three","prompt":"Differentiate $\\dfrac{2x+1}{x^{2}+3}$, simplifying the numerator.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(-2*x^2-2*x+6)/(x^2+3)^2"},"hints":["u = 2x + 1.","v = x² + 3.","Expand."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient","d":"$\\dfrac{2(x^{2}+3)-2x(2x+1)}{(x^{2}+3)^{2}}$"},{"h":"Simplify","d":"Expand the numerator"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient rule","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-274","group":"A11-C1-274","dp":"C1.3b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Reciprocal of a squared linear term","prompt":"Find the gradient of $y=\\dfrac1{(3x-2)^{2}}$ at $x=1$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-6},"hints":["Write as a negative power.","Chain rule.","Substitute."],"steps":[{"h":"Chain","d":"$-2(3x-2)^{-3}\\cdot3$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$-6(1)^{-3}$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Derivative","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"−6","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-285","group":"A11-C1-285","dp":"C1.3b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Quotient of x squared minus one over plus one","prompt":"Differentiate $y=\\dfrac{x^{2}-1}{x^{2}+1}$ and simplify.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"4*x/(x^2+1)^2"},"hints":["u = x² − 1.","v = x² + 1.","Factor 2x."],"steps":[{"h":"Quotient","d":"$\\dfrac{2x(x^{2}+1)-2x(x^{2}-1)}{(x^{2}+1)^{2}}$"},{"h":"Simplify","d":"$\\dfrac{4x}{(x^{2}+1)^{2}}$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient rule","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Simplified","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-286","group":"A11-C1-286","dp":"C1.3a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Rate of change of a cube's volume with its side","prompt":"Find the rate of change of the volume of a cube with respect to its side length when the side is $4$ cm.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":48},"hints":["V = s³.","Differentiate.","s = 4."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$3s^{2}$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"48","answer":true}]},{"id":"A11-C1-290","group":"A11-C1-290","dp":"C1.3b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Gradient of a fourth power of a quadratic","prompt":"Find the gradient of $y=(x^{2}-3x)^{4}$ at $x=1$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":32},"hints":["Outer power.","Inner derivative.","Substitute."],"steps":[{"h":"Chain","d":"$4(x^{2}-3x)^{3}(2x-3)$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$4(-2)^{3}(-1)$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Derivative","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"32","answer":true}]}]}
